1
00:00:02,002 --> 00:00:03,242
GORDON: <i>Previously on</i> Gotham...

2
00:00:03,270 --> 00:00:04,363
SOFIA: <i>Harvey is weak,</i>

3
00:00:04,471 --> 00:00:07,373
<i>and how many more cops need to
die because of his incompetence?</i>

4
00:00:07,508 --> 00:00:10,342
As of this moment, I'm assuming
the Captaincy of Gotham Central.

5
00:00:10,444 --> 00:00:12,037
Nothing in Gotham is free.

6
00:00:12,145 --> 00:00:14,740
You wanted a gangster to
help you get rid of Penguin.

7
00:00:14,848 --> 00:00:16,874
This is what that
help looks like.

8
00:00:16,984 --> 00:00:20,853
The whole town has gone
hog wild for the Pyg. (SNORTS)

9
00:00:21,255 --> 00:00:24,316
GORDON: <i>Turns out the Pyg's
real name is Lazlo Valentine.</i>

10
00:00:24,858 --> 00:00:26,258
<i>And he just escaped.</i>

11
00:00:26,360 --> 00:00:28,659
LEE: I haven't been looking
for a cure for your brain, Ed,

12
00:00:28,729 --> 00:00:30,039
because I was afraid
that if I told you the truth,

13
00:00:30,063 --> 00:00:31,998
<i>you would go back to
being who you were before.</i>

14
00:00:32,065 --> 00:00:34,057
<i>And I like who you've become.</i>

15
00:00:34,368 --> 00:00:36,030
BRUCE: <i>I'm not the
hero Gotham needs.</i>

16
00:00:36,203 --> 00:00:38,229
- I took the dark path.
- ALFRED: Yes, you did.

17
00:00:38,405 --> 00:00:41,204
<i>And it's gonna be a
long, bumpy journey back.</i>

18
00:00:41,508 --> 00:00:43,238
- What...
- Hello, Victor.

19
00:00:43,343 --> 00:00:45,608
- Where's the boy?
- SOFIA: Alive, for now.

20
00:00:45,946 --> 00:00:47,539
<i>If Oswald wants
to keep it that way,</i>

21
00:00:47,614 --> 00:00:49,674
<i>he will meet me under
the Crown Point Bridge...</i>

22
00:00:52,853 --> 00:00:56,790
You wanted a
war, you've got one!

23
00:00:58,392 --> 00:01:02,853
We will wait for Mr. Cobblepot
to send instructions.

24
00:01:03,030 --> 00:01:04,054
Ahh!

25
00:01:05,365 --> 00:01:06,560
(ALL GRUNTING)

26
00:01:16,710 --> 00:01:17,710
Hello.

27
00:01:22,449 --> 00:01:25,283
Where is Penguin, little man?

28
00:01:55,282 --> 00:01:58,411
This is Gordon. I need
forensics in West End Alley.

29
00:01:59,286 --> 00:02:02,688
A black-market
doc. Pyg was here.

30
00:02:03,023 --> 00:02:04,651
Looks like he got a new face.

31
00:02:04,992 --> 00:02:06,961
(CHOKING)

32
00:02:23,143 --> 00:02:24,143
(MR. PENN SCREAMING)

33
00:02:26,847 --> 00:02:30,215
So, Penguin's out building
support amongst the gangs.

34
00:02:30,484 --> 00:02:33,386
Pretty soon every criminal in
Gotham is gonna be hunting us.

35
00:02:34,021 --> 00:02:36,422
He's out building support
because we made him look weak.

36
00:02:36,857 --> 00:02:39,827
We kill him, and all the
gangs will support me.

37
00:02:40,293 --> 00:02:42,956
- I'm still a Falcone.
- Yeah, you mentioned that.

38
00:02:43,330 --> 00:02:44,992
- About a billion times.
- (DOOR OPENS)

39
00:02:50,671 --> 00:02:53,368
(EXHALES) He doesn't
know where Penguin is.

40
00:02:55,308 --> 00:02:56,640
(CELL PHONE VIBRATES)

41
00:02:57,077 --> 00:02:58,978
(SIGHS) What?

42
00:03:04,384 --> 00:03:05,443
I'll be right there.

43
00:03:06,720 --> 00:03:07,813
Is that about Penguin?

44
00:03:09,556 --> 00:03:10,556
No.

45
00:03:16,963 --> 00:03:18,022
Harper.

46
00:03:18,131 --> 00:03:20,896
We were an hour outside of Gotham
when I got waylaid by Victor Zsasz.

47
00:03:21,001 --> 00:03:24,267
He took Sofia. Gave me
this. I woke up in Virginia.

48
00:03:24,371 --> 00:03:26,272
Damn it. I had a
deal with Penguin.

49
00:03:26,373 --> 00:03:28,184
There's more. We're getting
word Penguin had some

50
00:03:28,208 --> 00:03:30,609
meeting under the Crown
Point Bridge late last night.

51
00:03:30,711 --> 00:03:34,341
Gunfire. A car blown up.
Sofia Falcone was there.

52
00:03:34,414 --> 00:03:36,440
All right, we have to
find Penguin. Harper?

53
00:03:36,550 --> 00:03:38,883
- I'm good, Cap.
- Put out a citywide BOLO.

54
00:03:38,985 --> 00:03:40,886
- I'll find Sofia.
- HARPER: What about the Pyg?

55
00:03:40,987 --> 00:03:44,583
- I heard he escaped from Arkham.
- Tracked him to a black market surgeon.

56
00:03:44,691 --> 00:03:47,593
He's already got a new
face. Lazlo Valentine is gone.

57
00:03:47,694 --> 00:03:50,061
- But if we don't find him...
- Focus on the bigger problem.

58
00:03:51,264 --> 00:03:52,755
We've got a war to stop, people.

59
00:04:01,575 --> 00:04:04,135
So, you're gonna tell us why
we're at your dad's house?

60
00:04:04,244 --> 00:04:05,244
Why do you think?

61
00:04:16,890 --> 00:04:17,890
Sofia.

62
00:04:22,195 --> 00:04:23,390
You look tired.

63
00:04:24,798 --> 00:04:27,165
Ms. Kean, it's good
to see you again.

64
00:04:28,401 --> 00:04:31,166
Likewise. So this is weird.

65
00:04:33,840 --> 00:04:35,001
Why are you here, Father?

66
00:04:36,176 --> 00:04:38,407
What did I tell you when you
asked to return to Gotham?

67
00:04:39,112 --> 00:04:40,876
- I know...
- (LOUDLY) What did I tell you?

68
00:04:43,216 --> 00:04:44,878
- That I wasn't ready.
- Exactly.

69
00:04:45,218 --> 00:04:47,278
And you came back anyway.

70
00:04:48,388 --> 00:04:51,790
Perhaps I should've acted
then. But I was indulgent.

71
00:04:51,892 --> 00:04:55,761
Curious. Who is this
daughter I raised?

72
00:04:57,697 --> 00:04:59,495
Father, Penguin is weak.

73
00:04:59,966 --> 00:05:01,298
If you help me, we can end this.

74
00:05:01,368 --> 00:05:03,337
I don't want Gotham.

75
00:05:03,503 --> 00:05:05,369
I don't believe that.
You love this city.

76
00:05:06,706 --> 00:05:07,935
I used to, yes.

77
00:05:09,709 --> 00:05:10,938
But I'm dying, Sofia.

78
00:05:12,412 --> 00:05:16,179
Someone else can have Gotham.
What I care about now is my family.

79
00:05:16,349 --> 00:05:21,014
And I'm your family. And I want this. I
deserve this. Gotham belongs to me.

80
00:05:24,958 --> 00:05:27,189
Your actions have
disgraced our family.

81
00:05:28,161 --> 00:05:29,891
Tell me how sleeping
with Jim Gordon,

82
00:05:29,996 --> 00:05:33,023
the man who killed your
brother, helped reclaim Gotham.

83
00:05:34,334 --> 00:05:35,334
I'm sorry, what?

84
00:05:35,569 --> 00:05:38,004
I have done many things
I will have to answer for.

85
00:05:38,371 --> 00:05:40,499
But I always knew
the meaning of honor.

86
00:05:42,475 --> 00:05:44,137
You have proven that you do not.

87
00:05:48,348 --> 00:05:49,348
Children... (CHUCKLES)

88
00:05:50,717 --> 00:05:53,812
- They can be such disappointments.
- (SELINA GASPS)

89
00:05:58,925 --> 00:06:01,053
I kill him, and this
is over. Please.

90
00:06:01,828 --> 00:06:03,729
You know why I came
when Penguin called?

91
00:06:04,431 --> 00:06:06,161
It's because you
were going to lose.

92
00:06:07,567 --> 00:06:09,502
If you were anyone
but my daughter,

93
00:06:10,437 --> 00:06:12,030
you'd be dead right now.

94
00:06:28,288 --> 00:06:30,018
Oh. Morning.

95
00:06:31,057 --> 00:06:32,081
In there.

96
00:06:34,194 --> 00:06:35,194
ALFRED: Dear, oh, dear.

97
00:06:37,063 --> 00:06:40,261
Oh. Good morning, Officer.
My name is Alfred Pennyworth.

98
00:06:40,767 --> 00:06:43,259
Neighbors called
in a noise complaint.

99
00:06:43,603 --> 00:06:45,401
- He's all yours.
- Thank you.

100
00:06:48,708 --> 00:06:49,708
Right.

101
00:06:56,249 --> 00:06:57,376
(SCOFFS)

102
00:07:01,821 --> 00:07:02,914
(ALL GASPING)

103
00:07:02,989 --> 00:07:05,151
- Good morning, Master Bruce.
- WOMAN: Oh, my God!

104
00:07:05,258 --> 00:07:07,386
I do believe the party
is well and truly over.

105
00:07:08,828 --> 00:07:11,093
Morning, miss.
Good morning, miss.

106
00:07:18,471 --> 00:07:19,471
GCPD.

107
00:07:20,073 --> 00:07:21,974
- I'm looking...
- For my daughter.

108
00:07:22,943 --> 00:07:25,412
You can stop. She's with me.

109
00:07:27,147 --> 00:07:28,147
GORDON: Carmine.

110
00:07:28,949 --> 00:07:30,349
I didn't expect to see you.

111
00:07:31,184 --> 00:07:33,278
I imagine not. I
arrived this morning.

112
00:07:34,087 --> 00:07:36,147
- You heard Sofia is in danger.
- Was in danger.

113
00:07:36,456 --> 00:07:37,788
I made a deal with Cobblepot.

114
00:07:38,692 --> 00:07:41,355
I take her out of Gotham
today and she lives.

115
00:07:42,095 --> 00:07:43,961
I made the same
deal, he didn't keep it.

116
00:07:44,764 --> 00:07:45,764
He will with me.

117
00:07:51,471 --> 00:07:52,905
I'm glad I never killed you.

118
00:07:55,475 --> 00:07:56,475
Thanks.

119
00:07:56,576 --> 00:07:59,671
Don't thank me. Killing you
would have been a kindness.

120
00:08:00,613 --> 00:08:02,878
You have no idea what
you've brought to your city.

121
00:08:03,516 --> 00:08:07,180
I imagine when you find out
the truth, it will destroy you.

122
00:08:09,789 --> 00:08:11,121
That's a comfort.

123
00:08:16,629 --> 00:08:21,329
Another day. Another man
sending me out of Gotham.

124
00:08:21,434 --> 00:08:23,198
We're both just trying
to keep you alive.

125
00:08:23,703 --> 00:08:25,035
Tell yourself that.

126
00:08:26,039 --> 00:08:28,770
But what I know is that
neither of you believed in me.

127
00:08:31,478 --> 00:08:32,707
Could have been so different.

128
00:08:41,688 --> 00:08:43,316
Goodbye, James Gordon.

129
00:08:53,199 --> 00:08:55,100
I doubt we'll see
each other again.

130
00:08:59,005 --> 00:09:00,735
The sun never shines here.

131
00:09:07,080 --> 00:09:09,413
Everything I did,
I did for your love.

132
00:09:11,718 --> 00:09:13,084
That doesn't matter, does it?

133
00:09:13,253 --> 00:09:15,745
What matters is that after
everything you've done,

134
00:09:17,023 --> 00:09:19,151
I still consider
you my daughter.

135
00:09:20,160 --> 00:09:21,423
That's enough.

136
00:09:26,366 --> 00:09:28,358
Mother planted those
roses, she loved them.

137
00:09:30,770 --> 00:09:32,500
I wanna take one with me.

138
00:09:59,766 --> 00:10:00,766
Get down!

139
00:10:18,384 --> 00:10:19,408
(GASPS)

140
00:10:33,800 --> 00:10:35,063
(INAUDIBLE)

141
00:10:46,379 --> 00:10:48,712
<i>Gotham is still reeling
from the violent death</i>

142
00:10:48,815 --> 00:10:51,046
<i>of Carmine Falcone
three days ago.</i>

143
00:10:51,151 --> 00:10:54,553
<i>Falcone ruled the Gotham
underworld for nearly 30 years.</i>

144
00:10:55,522 --> 00:10:57,684
<i>No arrests have been
made and a strange quiet...</i>

145
00:10:57,790 --> 00:10:59,520
Pleasant night, Master Bruce?

146
00:10:59,626 --> 00:11:02,994
There's a mess in the
Rolls. You'll need a bucket.

147
00:11:05,465 --> 00:11:08,196
MALE NEWSCASTER: <i>which many
have attributed to the Pax Penguina.</i>

148
00:11:08,301 --> 00:11:10,702
<i>Indeed, the Don's claim
to the throne of Gotham...</i>

149
00:11:10,803 --> 00:11:12,203
He shouldn't have come back.

150
00:11:12,305 --> 00:11:15,104
<i>More recent years by a
new breed of criminal...</i>

151
00:11:15,175 --> 00:11:17,440
<i>Leaving some to
ask, does Gotham...</i>

152
00:11:17,510 --> 00:11:18,773
Yes, Victor?

153
00:11:19,012 --> 00:11:22,608
You would've told me, right? If
you were gonna ice the old man.

154
00:11:22,682 --> 00:11:26,210
(SCOFFS) Obviously! Victor,
I did not kill Don Falcone.

155
00:11:26,319 --> 00:11:28,151
Well, everyone on the
street thinks you did.

156
00:11:28,221 --> 00:11:31,851
So let 'em. My hands are
clean. You have my word.

157
00:11:32,525 --> 00:11:34,203
MALE NEWSCASTER:
<i>With Don Falcone's passing,</i>

158
00:11:34,227 --> 00:11:37,322
<i>it is unknown how or indeed
when the void of power</i>

159
00:11:37,397 --> 00:11:40,424
<i>at the center of the city's
underworld will be filled.</i>

160
00:11:44,337 --> 00:11:46,067
(CHOIR SINGING)

161
00:12:08,962 --> 00:12:10,089
GORDON: Sofia.

162
00:12:12,232 --> 00:12:15,100
- I came to the hospital.
- I told them not to admit you.

163
00:12:16,603 --> 00:12:20,062
- I am truly sorry about your father.
- You know it was Penguin.

164
00:12:20,406 --> 00:12:23,205
And if I had evidence
supporting that, I'd arrest him.

165
00:12:23,443 --> 00:12:27,039
He is over there, waiting
to see my face and gloat.

166
00:12:27,780 --> 00:12:31,410
He is a liar. And a
murderer many times over.

167
00:12:32,619 --> 00:12:34,178
But you need evidence.

168
00:12:37,357 --> 00:12:38,950
I have to bury my father.

169
00:12:40,860 --> 00:12:42,158
Excuse us.

170
00:12:48,268 --> 00:12:49,268
(GASPS)

171
00:13:30,610 --> 00:13:31,610
Victor!

172
00:13:47,960 --> 00:13:50,555
- (SIGHS) Harvey.
- Jim.

173
00:13:51,531 --> 00:13:52,531
Your leave is almost up.

174
00:13:53,700 --> 00:13:56,499
- Be good to have you back.
- We'll see.

175
00:13:57,637 --> 00:13:59,437
So why haven't you
arrested the little weasel?

176
00:14:02,875 --> 00:14:04,468
Penguin still owns the judges.

177
00:14:04,977 --> 00:14:07,412
If I arrest him, and it's
not rock solid, he'll walk.

178
00:14:07,513 --> 00:14:10,039
So him whacking Falcone
and you sitting on your hands,

179
00:14:10,483 --> 00:14:12,213
what good does that do?

180
00:14:19,058 --> 00:14:22,460
It was Sofia who paid off the
Mayor to make me Captain.

181
00:14:22,995 --> 00:14:23,995
I didn't ask her to.

182
00:14:25,465 --> 00:14:26,524
Well, well.

183
00:14:26,699 --> 00:14:29,396
She's been pressing me to
move on Penguin. Even before this.

184
00:14:30,236 --> 00:14:31,236
I told you, didn't I?

185
00:14:32,472 --> 00:14:33,872
That bill would come due.

186
00:14:36,008 --> 00:14:39,206
I can't allow her to turn the
GCPD into her own private army.

187
00:14:39,312 --> 00:14:41,804
We've come too far.
This has to be by the book.

188
00:14:43,316 --> 00:14:44,750
Then forget Falcone.

189
00:14:46,018 --> 00:14:48,180
Penguin's too smart to
get nailed for that anyway.

190
00:14:49,689 --> 00:14:50,713
What do you mean?

191
00:14:51,224 --> 00:14:53,455
Get him to do something
you can really bust him for.

192
00:14:53,726 --> 00:14:56,628
And then yank his ass off
the street once and for all.

193
00:14:57,764 --> 00:15:00,256
- You're saying start a war.
- I'm saying get him to start one.

194
00:15:00,533 --> 00:15:01,899
You know he's
gonna come for her.

195
00:15:02,702 --> 00:15:04,432
I don't give a tinker's
damn about Sofia.

196
00:15:04,537 --> 00:15:06,081
Way I see it, everything
that's happened,

197
00:15:06,105 --> 00:15:08,233
down to Don Falcone
lying in that box,

198
00:15:08,408 --> 00:15:11,435
comes from you deciding
months ago to go after Penguin.

199
00:15:12,945 --> 00:15:14,140
This is all on you.

200
00:15:16,716 --> 00:15:18,412
So finish what you started.

201
00:15:30,763 --> 00:15:32,061
PENGUIN: Goodbye, old friend.

202
00:15:34,534 --> 00:15:36,901
I will not forget all
that you taught me.

203
00:15:46,946 --> 00:15:48,744
I had great respect
for your father.

204
00:15:50,483 --> 00:15:51,994
But once he's in
the ground, you are...

205
00:15:52,018 --> 00:15:53,850
- Excuse me.
- (BREATHES HEAVILY)

206
00:16:03,196 --> 00:16:04,289
Not here.

207
00:16:07,834 --> 00:16:09,427
What're you doing, Jim?

208
00:16:09,502 --> 00:16:10,936
Finishing what I started.

209
00:16:18,544 --> 00:16:20,240
(INDISTINCT CHATTERING)

210
00:16:30,656 --> 00:16:34,525
<i>Testing, testing, one,
two, three. James Gordon.</i>

211
00:16:35,962 --> 00:16:37,123
<i>James Gordon.</i>

212
00:16:39,799 --> 00:16:41,199
GORDON: What do
you want, Oswald?

213
00:16:42,502 --> 00:16:44,698
<i>You know what I
want. Where is she?</i>

214
00:16:45,605 --> 00:16:46,605
No.

215
00:16:47,540 --> 00:16:51,204
<i>You're seriously going
to go to war for her?</i>

216
00:16:51,310 --> 00:16:52,869
I'm upholding the law.

217
00:16:54,080 --> 00:16:57,050
No one gets to decide
who lives or dies in Gotham.

218
00:16:59,051 --> 00:17:02,920
<i>Can you not see, Jim? She's
manipulated you and lied...</i>

219
00:17:03,022 --> 00:17:04,650
The law is the law.

220
00:17:05,591 --> 00:17:09,187
Now either get over it or
face the consequences.

221
00:17:10,096 --> 00:17:11,325
(MICROPHONE FEEDBACK)

222
00:17:13,432 --> 00:17:14,695
Let's try it this way.

223
00:17:17,770 --> 00:17:21,707
Sofia Falcone is in this
building, whoever brings her to me

224
00:17:21,774 --> 00:17:23,800
will be richly rewarded.

225
00:17:23,876 --> 00:17:25,868
I'm going to count to five.

226
00:17:25,978 --> 00:17:27,222
Count as much
as you want, twerp.

227
00:17:27,246 --> 00:17:29,579
Yeah, we don't work for you.

228
00:17:32,018 --> 00:17:37,514
This man is asking you to risk
your lives to protect a gangster!

229
00:17:38,991 --> 00:17:41,654
I am offering you money. Huh?

230
00:17:41,827 --> 00:17:46,356
And bonus, no one
gets killed. (LAUGHS)

231
00:17:46,532 --> 00:17:48,728
Hey, Captain, can we?

232
00:17:49,168 --> 00:17:50,192
Sure.

233
00:17:51,404 --> 00:17:52,929
Get off me.

234
00:17:53,039 --> 00:17:57,477
Blood will run, Jim. Mark
my words! Blood will run!

235
00:17:57,577 --> 00:17:59,045
It will be on your hands!

236
00:17:59,612 --> 00:18:00,705
(PENGUIN YELLING)

237
00:18:01,147 --> 00:18:02,911
(OFFICERS JEERING)

238
00:18:11,490 --> 00:18:13,425
From the first day
I put on the badge,

239
00:18:15,294 --> 00:18:17,456
I was told things
could never change.

240
00:18:18,664 --> 00:18:22,624
Gotham was corrupt.
GCPD was corrupt.

241
00:18:24,170 --> 00:18:26,537
Criminals and
lowlifes ran things.

242
00:18:29,642 --> 00:18:31,440
You just showed me different.

243
00:18:33,713 --> 00:18:35,238
Penguin will be coming.

244
00:18:37,416 --> 00:18:39,749
It's time we showed
Gotham who we are.

245
00:18:43,389 --> 00:18:44,618
Suit up.

246
00:18:47,259 --> 00:18:48,625
(GUNS COCKING)

247
00:18:56,869 --> 00:18:58,428
(INDISTINCT SHOUTING)

248
00:19:30,936 --> 00:19:33,963
Just let us go. You've
obviously got your hands full.

249
00:19:34,674 --> 00:19:36,973
- Shut up!
- Whatever.

250
00:19:37,309 --> 00:19:38,971
They'll all be dead
in a few minutes.

251
00:19:39,679 --> 00:19:41,011
Listen, you stupid... (GROANS)

252
00:19:44,350 --> 00:19:45,750
(INDISTINCT CHATTER
ON LOUDSPEAKER)

253
00:19:46,218 --> 00:19:47,846
(GUNFIRE CONTINUES)

254
00:19:55,227 --> 00:19:56,286
More left.

255
00:19:58,698 --> 00:19:59,698
She means your left.

256
00:20:00,866 --> 00:20:01,993
Then say that.

257
00:20:06,839 --> 00:20:08,273
Your left! Your left! Your left!

258
00:20:11,877 --> 00:20:13,106
- Hmm.
- (SIGHS)

259
00:20:13,679 --> 00:20:14,679
Yay. Teamwork!

260
00:20:16,782 --> 00:20:19,013
(INDISTINCT CHATTERING)

261
00:20:21,253 --> 00:20:23,745
- SOFIA: You're winning.
- So far.

262
00:20:24,356 --> 00:20:26,689
But every gang in Gotham
owes Penguin allegiance.

263
00:20:27,426 --> 00:20:28,553
I can't arrest them all.

264
00:20:29,128 --> 00:20:31,063
So arrest Penguin,
wasn't that the point?

265
00:20:31,697 --> 00:20:34,257
As long as he's using
proxies, he's protected.

266
00:20:34,834 --> 00:20:36,359
I have to keep pressing him.

267
00:20:36,435 --> 00:20:37,869
When his back
is against the wall,

268
00:20:37,937 --> 00:20:40,600
he'll do something he
can't take back or explain.

269
00:20:40,706 --> 00:20:41,935
And then I'll have him.

270
00:20:42,041 --> 00:20:44,670
So, you're baiting him into
committing a public atrocity.

271
00:20:49,615 --> 00:20:50,947
What if he already has?

272
00:20:52,384 --> 00:20:56,913
There's this boy from my orphanage.
Martin. Oswald cared for him.

273
00:20:58,390 --> 00:21:00,188
I hid him away for his safety.

274
00:21:00,259 --> 00:21:04,822
But Oswald forced me into
telling him where Martin was,

275
00:21:05,598 --> 00:21:08,295
and then put him in
a car, and blew it up.

276
00:21:09,969 --> 00:21:11,733
Why didn't you
tell me this before?

277
00:21:12,471 --> 00:21:15,134
Because I'm his enemy.
Who's going to believe me?

278
00:21:15,241 --> 00:21:17,142
Also, I didn't see
him plant the bomb.

279
00:21:17,243 --> 00:21:19,178
- So you have nothing?
- I didn't say that.

280
00:21:20,079 --> 00:21:23,447
Oswald never understood the
way people cared for my father.

281
00:21:24,183 --> 00:21:26,311
And one of those
people just called me.

282
00:21:29,288 --> 00:21:31,257
How is Jim Gordon beating us?

283
00:21:31,490 --> 00:21:34,050
Well, every cop in
Gotham is behind him.

284
00:21:34,727 --> 00:21:36,889
I'm guessing he has
great leadership skills.

285
00:21:38,964 --> 00:21:41,058
Victor, when this
is said and done,

286
00:21:41,667 --> 00:21:46,435
you and I need to have a frank
discussion about chain of command.

287
00:21:47,673 --> 00:21:52,577
But now, go do something
horrific! Show the GCPD exactly...

288
00:21:52,645 --> 00:21:53,772
GORDON: Oswald Cobblepot,

289
00:21:55,447 --> 00:21:56,574
you're under arrest.

290
00:21:58,184 --> 00:22:00,244
Have you completely
lost your mind?

291
00:22:00,319 --> 00:22:02,618
Nobody has to die. We
only want Cobblepot!

292
00:22:02,688 --> 00:22:06,648
Well, see, Jim, that's a
problem, as they work for me.

293
00:22:07,393 --> 00:22:09,521
But just so I know,
what's the charge?

294
00:22:10,563 --> 00:22:11,563
Murder.

295
00:22:14,200 --> 00:22:18,035
Enough! Enough! I
did not kill Don Falcone!

296
00:22:18,137 --> 00:22:20,003
And I dare you to
prove otherwise.

297
00:22:20,072 --> 00:22:21,700
GORDON: It's not for Falcone.

298
00:22:21,807 --> 00:22:23,503
I'm arresting you for the murder

299
00:22:23,576 --> 00:22:26,307
of the boy you blew up
under the Crown Point Bridge.

300
00:22:28,314 --> 00:22:29,338
(SNICKERING)

301
00:22:30,749 --> 00:22:31,808
What's so funny?

302
00:22:33,719 --> 00:22:38,783
Nothing. Well, everything,
actually, 'cause you see,

303
00:22:39,358 --> 00:22:41,452
he's not dead. (LAUGHS)

304
00:22:42,862 --> 00:22:46,321
I only faked his death
so that Sofia Falcone

305
00:22:46,398 --> 00:22:48,128
couldn't use him against me.

306
00:22:49,635 --> 00:22:51,146
She's the one who told
you I killed him, isn't she?

307
00:22:51,170 --> 00:22:52,170
Then where is he?

308
00:22:54,640 --> 00:22:58,077
(STAMMERS) I don't know. Victor
took him out of Gotham, tell him.

309
00:22:58,811 --> 00:22:59,811
ZSASZ: What's to tell?

310
00:23:02,748 --> 00:23:04,910
You blew that kid sky-high.

311
00:23:07,453 --> 00:23:08,512
PENGUIN: What?

312
00:23:09,421 --> 00:23:12,084
You sent that pipsqueak
to kingdom come.

313
00:23:12,558 --> 00:23:14,754
No! That's not true!

314
00:23:15,227 --> 00:23:16,855
And I'll testify to that.

315
00:23:17,863 --> 00:23:18,863
What?

316
00:23:19,298 --> 00:23:22,200
Look, I ain't taking the
rap for no kid murder.

317
00:23:23,769 --> 00:23:25,247
- (YELLS)
- GORDON: Get him out of here!

318
00:23:25,271 --> 00:23:28,969
You are lying! You
are a lying traitor!

319
00:23:29,074 --> 00:23:33,535
Victor Zsasz is a
liar! No! I will kill you!

320
00:23:33,612 --> 00:23:34,612
Traitor!

321
00:23:36,548 --> 00:23:40,110
GORDON: This doesn't give
you a free pass, you know.

322
00:23:41,053 --> 00:23:42,053
Jim...

323
00:23:44,423 --> 00:23:45,550
Not now.

324
00:24:03,542 --> 00:24:05,977
You did it, Cap. You won.

325
00:24:13,185 --> 00:24:14,448
(CHEERING)

326
00:24:24,129 --> 00:24:27,258
So I'm guessing Gordon doesn't
know the kid's actually alive.

327
00:24:27,800 --> 00:24:29,132
Jim Gordon played his part.

328
00:24:29,201 --> 00:24:31,602
He showed the underworld
that Penguin was weak.

329
00:24:31,837 --> 00:24:34,363
That he did. End of the day...

330
00:24:36,275 --> 00:24:37,275
He's a Cobblepot.

331
00:24:39,578 --> 00:24:40,739
You are a Falcone.

332
00:24:48,821 --> 00:24:52,019
Smile, ladies. It's a new day.

333
00:24:57,997 --> 00:25:02,492
So, Sofia was as good as
her word, we got our club back.

334
00:25:03,102 --> 00:25:05,662
Yippee. We get to
serve drinks again.

335
00:25:06,472 --> 00:25:08,168
It's just a base of operations.

336
00:25:08,607 --> 00:25:12,567
But I am meeting with the designer
later to make it less Penguiny.

337
00:25:13,479 --> 00:25:14,708
Have fun.

338
00:25:16,215 --> 00:25:17,979
Music to soothe
the savage beast?

339
00:25:19,551 --> 00:25:20,849
Something like that.

340
00:25:32,731 --> 00:25:33,731
Alfred?

341
00:25:36,168 --> 00:25:37,602
Oh, the front page is up?

342
00:25:38,904 --> 00:25:40,344
Didn't expect you
to brave the light

343
00:25:40,372 --> 00:25:42,500
of the day for couple
more hours, Master B.

344
00:25:43,075 --> 00:25:47,035
Tommy wanted to go to the
horse races. What's all this?

345
00:25:48,414 --> 00:25:50,076
It's a little project of mine.

346
00:25:50,182 --> 00:25:52,583
I like to call it, Operation
Save Bruce Wayne.

347
00:25:53,152 --> 00:25:54,381
(SCOFFS)

348
00:25:54,486 --> 00:25:55,579
Switzerland.

349
00:25:55,687 --> 00:25:57,918
Few months up in the
Alps, you'll be tickety-boo.

350
00:25:59,925 --> 00:26:01,257
Are you going to kidnap me?

351
00:26:02,394 --> 00:26:05,091
No, I'm going to appeal
to your better angels.

352
00:26:06,231 --> 00:26:08,257
And if that doesn't
work, I shall beg.

353
00:26:09,568 --> 00:26:11,059
Please, Master Bruce.

354
00:26:13,605 --> 00:26:15,301
If for no other
reason, do it for me.

355
00:26:22,381 --> 00:26:25,579
These past weeks, you know how
much I've thought about Ra's al Ghul?

356
00:26:26,151 --> 00:26:29,315
About my parents?
Not at all, Alfred.

357
00:26:30,089 --> 00:26:33,924
- All you're offering me is pain.
- Well, there is no life without pain.

358
00:26:34,159 --> 00:26:35,821
There's no love,
there is no joy.

359
00:26:35,928 --> 00:26:38,073
I don't know about that. I
am having a fair amount of joy.

360
00:26:38,097 --> 00:26:40,589
You're bloody miserable is
what you are, mate. I can see it.

361
00:26:42,501 --> 00:26:44,060
Alfred, I know
you care about me.

362
00:26:45,904 --> 00:26:48,703
But I am asking you to
stop what you are doing.

363
00:26:49,441 --> 00:26:50,875
I'm not who you thought I was.

364
00:26:50,943 --> 00:26:52,912
I'm not who my parents
might've wanted me to be.

365
00:26:53,145 --> 00:26:55,307
- And I'm okay with that.
- But I'm not okay with it.

366
00:26:56,048 --> 00:26:58,313
- And I don't believe it.
- And that's your problem.

367
00:26:59,718 --> 00:27:01,050
Now, I'm gonna go meet Tommy.

368
00:27:03,155 --> 00:27:04,595
Can't let you do
that, Master Bruce.

369
00:27:08,160 --> 00:27:09,219
(SIGHS)

370
00:27:12,164 --> 00:27:13,462
You gonna stop me?

371
00:27:15,100 --> 00:27:17,092
- If need be, yes.
- (SCOFFS)

372
00:27:21,640 --> 00:27:23,040
You really think you can?

373
00:27:24,042 --> 00:27:25,042
Oh, I know I can.

374
00:27:26,845 --> 00:27:28,507
I just don't want
you to make me try.

375
00:27:30,616 --> 00:27:31,616
Well...

376
00:27:32,818 --> 00:27:33,877
(BOTH GRUNTING)

377
00:27:34,019 --> 00:27:35,612
(OBJECTS CLATTERING)

378
00:27:36,688 --> 00:27:37,951
Don't do this, Master Bruce.

379
00:27:38,023 --> 00:27:39,855
No, Alfred, we're doing this.

380
00:27:40,526 --> 00:27:41,824
(BOTH GRUNTING)

381
00:27:48,300 --> 00:27:50,940
Getting slayed, Master Bruce.
Haven't been training, have you, son?

382
00:27:51,870 --> 00:27:53,338
- Got a bit of ring rust.
- Really?

383
00:27:54,506 --> 00:27:56,600
Because you're the only
one breathing hard, old man.

384
00:27:59,478 --> 00:28:00,605
(GROANS)

385
00:28:01,780 --> 00:28:07,151
- Stop it, will ya? Stop it! Stop!
- Fine! Fine.

386
00:28:12,558 --> 00:28:16,962
Oh, no. Master Bruce, I'm so sorry.
I don't know what came over me...

387
00:28:19,865 --> 00:28:20,889
(DOOR CLOSES)

388
00:28:23,035 --> 00:28:24,401
I am in control.

389
00:28:24,536 --> 00:28:25,595
(LAUGHS)

390
00:28:25,704 --> 00:28:29,106
I am in control. Me. Ed Nygma.

391
00:28:29,341 --> 00:28:30,461
But why would you want that?

392
00:28:30,542 --> 00:28:31,908
You don't understand.

393
00:28:32,010 --> 00:28:34,241
We had so much
fun when we were me.

394
00:28:35,214 --> 00:28:36,910
Oh, no.

395
00:28:37,549 --> 00:28:39,415
Tell me it's not that.

396
00:28:40,285 --> 00:28:41,285
Not what?

397
00:28:41,386 --> 00:28:43,753
I leave when
spurned. I give all.

398
00:28:43,855 --> 00:28:47,257
I take nothing. I can raise you to
a king, or make you to a beggar.

399
00:28:47,359 --> 00:28:48,554
What am I?

400
00:28:50,596 --> 00:28:52,929
I'm just gonna tell you 'cause
you're not going to get it.

401
00:28:53,198 --> 00:28:55,190
- Love.
- I am in control!

402
00:28:55,267 --> 00:28:57,896
You're in love with Lee
Thompkins, you pathetic loser.

403
00:28:58,003 --> 00:28:59,335
Shut up!

404
00:29:03,175 --> 00:29:06,043
Ed angry at mirror?

405
00:29:06,111 --> 00:29:08,171
No, Grundy. I am
not angry at the mirror.

406
00:29:08,947 --> 00:29:13,351
- Ed angry at Ed?
- That is...

407
00:29:15,354 --> 00:29:16,879
Surprisingly perceptive.

408
00:29:18,423 --> 00:29:20,392
(SIGHS) I need some air.

409
00:29:22,094 --> 00:29:23,426
(DOOR CLOSES)

410
00:29:29,001 --> 00:29:30,833
(MUSIC PLAYING ON GRAMOPHONE)

411
00:29:36,942 --> 00:29:41,107
<i>This was the end
of Solomon Grundy</i>

412
00:29:54,593 --> 00:29:55,652
Huh?

413
00:29:56,461 --> 00:29:57,554
(GROANS)

414
00:29:58,463 --> 00:30:02,594
<i>This was the end
of Solomon Grundy</i>

415
00:30:07,139 --> 00:30:11,474
<i>This was the end
of Solomon Grundy</i>

416
00:30:19,951 --> 00:30:21,647
(GRUNTING)

417
00:30:28,960 --> 00:30:31,361
- Where is Grundy?
- I kidnapped you.

418
00:30:32,364 --> 00:30:34,162
For the record,
you're not light.

419
00:30:36,535 --> 00:30:37,901
What pretty lady want?

420
00:30:42,474 --> 00:30:45,376
When we were fighting, you
called me "Tabby," remember?

421
00:30:46,878 --> 00:30:49,814
- Grundy want to go back to friend Ed.
- Ed...

422
00:30:51,083 --> 00:30:53,143
Right, your friend.

423
00:30:54,853 --> 00:30:57,789
Well, your best friend Ed
tied you and me to chairs,

424
00:30:57,856 --> 00:31:00,451
electrocuted you,
and cut off my hand.

425
00:31:01,626 --> 00:31:04,152
Look at the scar. Ring a bell?

426
00:31:09,234 --> 00:31:10,293
(EXHALES)

427
00:31:18,343 --> 00:31:23,304
Remember me, Butch. I'm Tabby.

428
00:31:25,417 --> 00:31:26,715
I'm your Tabby.

429
00:31:34,726 --> 00:31:35,887
Grundy sorry.

430
00:31:43,468 --> 00:31:44,731
Yeah. I'm sorry too.

431
00:31:52,043 --> 00:31:55,536
Before, when you said my
name, I'd just hit you in the head.

432
00:31:57,849 --> 00:31:58,908
Maybe that's the only way.

433
00:32:03,288 --> 00:32:04,916
So you're gonna
remember me, Butch...

434
00:32:08,693 --> 00:32:10,525
Or I'm gonna beat your head in.

435
00:32:12,464 --> 00:32:14,262
- Pretty lady...
- (GRUNTS)

436
00:32:22,040 --> 00:32:23,872
When I called, I wasn't
sure you would come.

437
00:32:24,075 --> 00:32:26,510
I was going to anyway.
We need to talk.

438
00:32:30,649 --> 00:32:31,649
I agree.

439
00:32:32,651 --> 00:32:34,847
I'm going to ask you not to
do what you're about to do.

440
00:32:34,953 --> 00:32:36,114
Which is?

441
00:32:36,588 --> 00:32:37,749
Unify the gangs.

442
00:32:38,490 --> 00:32:40,584
Put the Falcones back in
charge of the underworld.

443
00:32:42,127 --> 00:32:43,686
But wasn't that our deal?

444
00:32:44,196 --> 00:32:46,756
I'd replace Penguin. You'd
be the law, I'd be the order?

445
00:32:46,832 --> 00:32:51,361
No. And if you try and take
over, I'll have to come after you.

446
00:32:56,708 --> 00:33:00,645
James. You're nothing
if not predictable.

447
00:33:01,012 --> 00:33:03,641
(CLICKS TONGUE) Now, I think
it's time you heard my proposal.

448
00:33:03,748 --> 00:33:05,910
- I'm not interested.
- I think you are.

449
00:33:06,184 --> 00:33:07,184
MAN: Surprise.

450
00:33:07,686 --> 00:33:08,686
(GUN COCKS)

451
00:33:11,790 --> 00:33:14,783
I know, you thought I'd have

452
00:33:14,860 --> 00:33:16,852
a different face because
I killed that doctor.

453
00:33:18,163 --> 00:33:19,995
But that was just to
throw you off the scent.

454
00:33:20,665 --> 00:33:23,100
That's not why he's
surprised, Lazlo.

455
00:33:27,639 --> 00:33:28,902
THE PYG: Can I tell him?

456
00:33:30,008 --> 00:33:32,739
You came to this beautiful
woman because you had a problem.

457
00:33:33,044 --> 00:33:37,243
A Penguin problem. Pax
Penguina was gonna last.

458
00:33:38,383 --> 00:33:40,579
But Sofia had an idea.

459
00:33:41,253 --> 00:33:44,417
I'd heard of a contract killer that
was impersonating serial killers, so.

460
00:33:44,523 --> 00:33:48,688
What if there was a killer,
a real vicious son of a bitch,

461
00:33:48,760 --> 00:33:52,595
hunting the police,
all slice and dice.

462
00:33:52,998 --> 00:33:54,175
SOFIA: I needed the
police to turn on Penguin.

463
00:33:54,199 --> 00:33:56,566
I knew a few cops
would have to die.

464
00:33:56,668 --> 00:33:58,864
So you sent this
monster to my city?

465
00:34:00,739 --> 00:34:02,503
I let him improvise.

466
00:34:02,974 --> 00:34:05,170
I'll admit, got a
little carried away

467
00:34:05,243 --> 00:34:08,577
with the whole (CHUCKLES)
"cooking folks" routine.

468
00:34:10,649 --> 00:34:12,345
I really got in the role.

469
00:34:13,985 --> 00:34:17,478
You know, only hiccup was
that mess with her daddy.

470
00:34:24,329 --> 00:34:25,490
That was you.

471
00:34:27,198 --> 00:34:29,258
I gave him a chance, Jim.

472
00:34:30,035 --> 00:34:34,029
And if he would've shown
one iota of appreciation

473
00:34:34,105 --> 00:34:36,700
for everything I have
done for this family,

474
00:34:36,975 --> 00:34:39,945
for him... He would be alive.

475
00:34:40,445 --> 00:34:41,606
GORDON: But I saw you shot.

476
00:34:45,750 --> 00:34:47,378
There was another shooter there.

477
00:34:51,623 --> 00:34:53,888
SOFIA: <i>I had to do something
to throw off suspicion.</i>

478
00:34:54,159 --> 00:34:55,736
THE PYG: <i>Well, she
wasn't about to get herself</i>

479
00:34:55,760 --> 00:34:57,752
plugged by a bunch
of yahoos in a car.

480
00:34:58,930 --> 00:35:00,956
It was some pretty
shooting, if I do say so.

481
00:35:01,800 --> 00:35:03,928
I missed all her vital parts.

482
00:35:07,906 --> 00:35:10,933
I'm putting you in jail.
And this time it's Blackgate.

483
00:35:11,042 --> 00:35:13,307
- You are gonna rot in there.
- Jim...

484
00:35:13,411 --> 00:35:14,572
(GUNSHOT)

485
00:35:17,048 --> 00:35:18,380
(INHALES DEEPLY)

486
00:35:18,450 --> 00:35:19,645
That's done now.

487
00:35:24,089 --> 00:35:25,113
(CLATTERS)

488
00:35:25,223 --> 00:35:27,920
My father had his moment
of truth. This is yours.

489
00:35:30,562 --> 00:35:33,999
How many cops died under
the Pax Penguina? Not one.

490
00:35:34,799 --> 00:35:36,825
It was you who
couldn't stomach it.

491
00:35:37,702 --> 00:35:40,035
It was you who came
to the Falcones for help.

492
00:35:41,006 --> 00:35:43,498
There is a direct line
from your decision

493
00:35:43,608 --> 00:35:46,635
to a dozen police officers who
have been brutally murdered.

494
00:35:47,512 --> 00:35:48,512
You are insane.

495
00:35:50,515 --> 00:35:51,515
Why not just kill me?

496
00:35:52,183 --> 00:35:53,183
Because, Jim...

497
00:35:54,152 --> 00:35:56,212
I need you at the
head of the GCPD.

498
00:35:56,821 --> 00:35:58,813
- I need...
- Someone you can control.

499
00:36:00,625 --> 00:36:03,060
You've been planning this
since the day we first met.

500
00:36:04,863 --> 00:36:07,128
This isn't about
Gotham. This is revenge.

501
00:36:08,133 --> 00:36:09,533
For me killing Mario.

502
00:36:15,640 --> 00:36:16,972
(GUN THUDS)

503
00:36:18,443 --> 00:36:20,810
You want to arrest
me, arrest me.

504
00:36:23,448 --> 00:36:24,609
But I will talk.

505
00:36:26,351 --> 00:36:30,118
And the cops that died,
the friend that you betrayed,

506
00:36:30,188 --> 00:36:31,850
will all have been for nothing.

507
00:36:34,025 --> 00:36:35,823
The GCPD will crumble.

508
00:36:37,028 --> 00:36:38,587
Penguin, or someone worse,

509
00:36:38,697 --> 00:36:42,498
will take over and you
will lose Gotham forever.

510
00:36:45,036 --> 00:36:48,768
Or, take on the sin as your own.

511
00:36:51,076 --> 00:36:54,012
Keep the GCPD. Let
them think you're a hero.

512
00:36:54,546 --> 00:36:57,607
But live knowing who
you are. What you've done.

513
00:36:59,451 --> 00:37:01,113
That's my revenge.

514
00:37:07,926 --> 00:37:08,926
(PHONE BEEPS)

515
00:37:13,531 --> 00:37:14,760
FEMALE OFFICER: <i>GCPD.</i>

516
00:37:16,367 --> 00:37:18,199
<i>GCPD, how can I help you?</i>

517
00:37:19,838 --> 00:37:22,273
<i>Hello? Anyone there? Anybody?</i>

518
00:37:22,373 --> 00:37:23,671
This is Gordon.

519
00:37:24,676 --> 00:37:26,577
I'm at Sofia Falcone's...

520
00:37:28,713 --> 00:37:30,375
I just shot and killed the Pyg.

521
00:37:44,295 --> 00:37:47,390
Oh, thank Christ. You're safe.

522
00:37:48,299 --> 00:37:51,167
Master Bruce, listen, I
don't want to fight anymore.

523
00:37:53,238 --> 00:37:54,238
You win.

524
00:37:55,840 --> 00:37:57,638
If this is how you want to deal

525
00:37:57,742 --> 00:37:59,487
with what you've been
going through, then so be it.

526
00:37:59,511 --> 00:38:00,911
I'm not gonna try and stop you.

527
00:38:02,947 --> 00:38:03,947
But just know this...

528
00:38:06,518 --> 00:38:07,986
You will remember who you are,

529
00:38:08,086 --> 00:38:10,317
and when you do,
I will be right here...

530
00:38:10,421 --> 00:38:12,652
No, you won't be.

531
00:38:14,225 --> 00:38:16,626
I went to my lawyer and had
him draw up emancipation papers.

532
00:38:21,166 --> 00:38:22,634
You're no longer
my legal guardian.

533
00:38:30,775 --> 00:38:31,775
I won't sign them.

534
00:38:32,277 --> 00:38:35,645
You don't have to.
Now I'm going out.

535
00:38:36,981 --> 00:38:38,159
If you're still here
when I get back,

536
00:38:38,183 --> 00:38:40,015
I'll go to the police
and show them my face.

537
00:38:43,221 --> 00:38:45,349
- Master Bruce, please...
- Alfred, you're fired.

538
00:38:47,659 --> 00:38:49,218
Now get the hell
out of my house.

539
00:38:54,199 --> 00:38:56,293
(DOOR CLOSES)

540
00:39:05,343 --> 00:39:06,504
(PANTING)

541
00:39:08,313 --> 00:39:11,374
Butch! Say something!

542
00:39:16,154 --> 00:39:17,349
Say something.

543
00:39:20,692 --> 00:39:21,819
(PIPE CLATTERS)

544
00:39:22,026 --> 00:39:23,187
(GROANS)

545
00:39:25,964 --> 00:39:27,364
I'm sorry.

546
00:39:33,504 --> 00:39:34,699
I tried.

547
00:39:57,729 --> 00:39:59,061
(LAUGHING)

548
00:40:26,925 --> 00:40:28,257
(INDISTINCT CHATTERING)

549
00:40:55,987 --> 00:40:56,987
Harvey.

550
00:40:57,655 --> 00:40:59,681
I was just, uh,
dropping something off.

551
00:41:00,858 --> 00:41:03,987
Oh, I heard you got the Pyg.

552
00:41:04,862 --> 00:41:06,330
- And Penguin.
- Yeah.

553
00:41:07,498 --> 00:41:10,332
So everything turned out well.

554
00:41:10,435 --> 00:41:13,496
- You didn't even need me...
- You got a second? Could we, uh...

555
00:41:15,173 --> 00:41:19,975
They, uh, believe in
you. Don't let them down.

556
00:41:56,080 --> 00:41:57,480
What the hell happened to me?

557
00:42:02,186 --> 00:42:06,419
PENGUIN: Traitors.
Every single one of them.

558
00:42:08,326 --> 00:42:11,888
I'll kill her! I will
flay her alive!

559
00:42:12,530 --> 00:42:16,023
Her and Gordon and Zsasz and...

560
00:42:16,100 --> 00:42:17,363
(BANGING)

561
00:42:17,435 --> 00:42:19,529
- MAN: Hey, buddy...
- (GASPS)

562
00:42:21,239 --> 00:42:24,869
- Do not talk to me.
- I get it, pal...

563
00:42:25,343 --> 00:42:28,006
This place is full of loonies.

564
00:42:28,646 --> 00:42:31,548
I just thought, we could
help each other out.

565
00:42:34,318 --> 00:42:37,550
And how can you
help me? (CHUCKLES)

566
00:42:37,655 --> 00:42:44,186
Well, not to toot my own horn,
but I'm a very resourceful fellow.

567
00:42:44,262 --> 00:42:47,323
So, toot. Toot, toot!

568
00:42:48,332 --> 00:42:49,698
(MAN CACKLES)

569
00:42:50,268 --> 00:42:51,395
(GASPS)

570
00:42:51,469 --> 00:42:52,767
I know that laugh.

571
00:42:53,137 --> 00:42:56,574
What do you say, pal?
I'll be your best friend.

572
00:42:56,974 --> 00:42:58,408
(GASPS)

573
00:43:00,278 --> 00:43:01,746
Give me a smile...

574
00:43:02,647 --> 00:43:03,910
(LAUGHS)

575
00:43:45,289 --> 00:43:46,289
English - SDH
